Стажант – Технически сътрудник (WordPress / OpenCart)
Интернет реклама - Варна ООД помага на бизнеса, като създава цялостна концепция за развитие в онлайн пространството.
Имаме над 15 годишен опит на българския и международния пазар.
Фирмата се развива с бързи темпове и се нуждаем от креативни хора готови да усвоят нови знания и умения.
Искаш да се развиваш в сферата на уеб технологиите и дигиталния бизнес? Ние ще ти дадем шанс да го направиш!
Търсим мотивиран човек с базови технически познания, който иска да натрупа реален практически опит в поддръжката и развитието на уебсайтове и онлайн магазини.
Всеки кандидат с желание за развитие ще получи обучение и подкрепа от нашия екип. Ще имаш възможност да работиш по реални клиентски проекти и да развиваш практически умения в WordPress и OpenCart.
Какво търсим:
Базови познания и опит с WordPress;
Базови познания и опит с OpenCart;
Добра компютърна грамотност;
Интерес към уеб технологии и техническа поддръжка на сайтове;
Амбиция и желание за учене и развитие;
Способност за работа в екип и добра организация;
Владеенето на английски език ще се счита за предимство;
Подходящо образование в сферата на информационните технологии ще се счита за предимство;
Позицията е подходяща за кандидати без професионален опит по специалността.
Какво ще правиш:
Поддръжка на сайтове, разработени на WordPress и OpenCart;
Качване и редактиране на съдържание и продукти;
Работа с плъгини, модули и различни функционалности;
Извършване на базови технически настройки;
Съдействие при възникнали технически казуси;
Работа по реални проекти на наши клиенти.
Какво предлагаме:
Обучение и стаж по програма;
Практически опит с реални уеб проекти;
Подкрепа и обучение от опитен екип;
Добри условия на труд в спокойна работна среда;
Нормално работно време;
Възможност за кариерно и финансово развитие;
Възможност за постоянна работа след успешно завършване на стажа.
Искаш да превърнеш познанията си в WordPress и OpenCart в професионален опит?
Изпрати ни своето CV и стани част от екипа ни.

Senior Fullstack Java (Angular) Developer
Senior Fullstack Java (Angular) Developer
Varna/hybrid
Highly competitive salary and bonus and unbeatable benefits package
Nordic Recruitment & Consulting offers efficient IT and Cyber Security recruitment and business consulting in Bulgaria - and beyond.
Having long experience in recruitment we value above all those things that make us successful because of our clients, candidates and partners success: trustworthiness, good communication, Can do-attitude, finding solutions, being flexible; being available. We also have genuine passion for what we do.
The client is a leading financial group and Forbes2000 member. The company provides services in multiple domains, including Anti-Money Laundering, Accounts controlling, Business Solutions Competence, Credits, Financing, and other business domains. Since 2021 the group has been going through enhanced digital transformation, demanding software development, QA, AI, Cyber Security and other IT solutions.
As our Java (Angular) developer, you would have the following responsibilities:
Develop frontend and backend code for website applications within the AEM (Adobe Experience Manager – it is similar to WordPress) environment;
Integrate AEM with backend services (Spring Boot and microservices REST APIs and databases)
Maintain and upgrade our systems, ensuring high performance and security;
Collaborate with graphic designers for web design features;
Work through a project from concept to final product;
Work in Agile (SAFe) environment, in which we incrementally towards a tangible result.
Key competences that will help you succeed:
4+ years of experience with Java, Spring, Spring Boot and Maven;
Familiarity with HTML, CSS, JavaScript; AngularTS;
Experience working with REST API, JSON, HTTP;
Experience with Jenkins, Kubernetes/OpenShift, Tomcat and Gitflow.
You are a perfect fit for us if you:
Speak and write English fluently;
Have good technical and development skills;
Work and think customer- and solution-oriented;
Work pragmatically, even in time-critical circumstances;
Are open-minded, willing to learn continuously and open to innovation;
Are a real team player: working together in international multidisciplinary teams on a common result gives you energy;
Are enthusiastic, driven and always want to improve. You like to take initiative and are good at making connections.
Nordic Recruitment & Consulting's recruitment rights and activities are based upon Recruitment Licence No. 2022 (issued 01.04.2016). Services of Nordic Recruitment & Consulting are fully free for the candidates.

At CSoft we specialise in developing technological solutions for the banking and financial sector — for over 30 years our software has supported the daily operations of institutions in Bulgaria and beyond, from core banking processes to digital banking channels. Our team is built of people who take their seriously, help each other out and find a way to have fun along the way.
WHAT YOU WILL DO:
You'll join our team in Varna, working across our banking products (BrightOS, bDigital) and our internal engineering tooling — bringing AI into both where it earns its place.
Build AI features into our banking products end-to-end — design, build, evaluate, ship (e.g. document understanding, in-product assistants, exception/anomaly triage).
Automate internal engineering and ops workflows with LLMs and agents — code-review assistance, test and documentation generation, ticket triage, internal data tasks.
Establish AI-assisted development practices across teams — patterns, guardrails, and tooling around the coding harnesses we already use.
Own integrations fully: prompt and agent design, API integration, evaluation harnesses, and ongoing monitoring of output quality and cost.
Prototype fast, then harden what works into supported tools — keeping experiments and production clearly separated.
Do all of the above in a team for which Clean Architecture does not mean "cleaned building" and Design Language is not the that designers speak.
JOINS US - HERE'S WHAT YOU'LL GET:
The craft
Attractive payment, updated according to your progress;
Acquire invaluable professional skills;
Ongoing trainings to improve your professional skills and personal qualities (we will help you to grow, but we also expect proactivity on your part);
Opportunity to become part of a united and friendly team.
The comfort
Additional health insurance and stimulus to do sports actively (yes, your health is important for us);
Excellent working atmosphere in one of the longest-lasting software companies in Bulgaria;
Modern offices in a well-connected locations in the city;
Participation in conferences;
Balance between your professional and personal commitments, supplemented by flexible working hours;
A chance to participate in various CSR initiatives and do more for a better world;
Multiple thematic events (what about a chocolate party at the office or a SPA team building).
WE WOULD LIKE TO INVITE YOU IF YOU:
Cover these essentials:
Have strong general software engineering skills and ship production code independently;
Have demonstrated experience integrating LLMs or building agent workflows — prompting, RAG, tool/function calling, evaluation;
Are comfortable with APIs, automation, and integrating systems;
Have sound instincts around security and sensitive-data handling;
Have at least 5 years of experience in software development.
Even better if you:
Have experience building internal developer tooling or platforms;
Are familiar with LLM evaluation and observability — eval frameworks, tracing, cost monitoring.
Sound like you? Send us your CV!
We look forward to meeting you — and if this isn't quite your role, check our other openings.
All applications are treated in full confidentiality and in accordance with applicable regulations. Only shortlisted candidates will be invited to an interview. By applying, you voluntarily provide your personal data and consent to CSoft JSC processing it for the purposes of this selection.

CAD Data Developer with German and English
ImpacT Hire is actively seeking a CAD Data Developer with German and English for one of our clients — a leading international company specializing in professional software solutions for planning, design, and manufacturing in the furniture and interior design industry.
The role focuses on working with CAD/CAM (AutoCAD-based) software to implement and configure digital product data and technical specifications for a well-established German partner. You will contribute to building structured digital catalogs and 3D models used directly in real manufacturing and production environments.
This position is ideal for candidates with an engineering or technical background who enjoy working with CAD systems, structured data, and precise technical implementation.
Responsibilities:
➢ Work with imos CAD/CAM software to configure and implement furniture design and manufacturing solutions;
➢ Develop and maintain 3D models and technical data based on predefined customer specifications;
➢ Create and structure furniture hardware and product data, including components from a wide range of partner products;
➢ Support the development of online product catalogs and digital libraries used in design and production processes;
➢ Document development workflows, standards, and project requirements in the internal content management system;
➢ Collaborate closely with internal engineering and project teams to ensure accuracy and consistency of technical data.
Requirements:
➢ Fluency in German and English (minimum B2 level, written and spoken);
➢ Higher education completed or in progress (Bachelor’s or Master’s) in Engineering, Automation, Computer Systems, Industrial Design, or related technical field;
➢ Basic understanding or interest in CAD/CAM or technical design software;
➢ Good computer literacy and confidence working with modern digital tools.
Nice to Have:
➢ Experience with CAD software (AutoCAD, imos, SolidWorks, or similar);
➢ Experience working with technical or product data;
➢ Background in manufacturing, engineering design, or production processes.
What We Offer:
➢ Exciting tasks in a secure, international company offering diverse career perspectives;
➢ Comprehensive training and onboarding programs to get you started (no prior imos experience required);
➢ Home office options — up to 5 days per month;
➢ Standard working hours with no shift ;
➢ Opportunity to on real-world engineering and production solutions.
Work Location:
➢ The office is located in Varna, Bulgaria, and on-site is required.
If you are detail-oriented, technically minded, and interested in working with CAD systems and engineering data in an international environment, we’d love to hear from you.
ImpacT Hire has License №3355/13.07.2022 for providing HR services.

